  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORE FUNDING TO MISEAN CARA, WHICH PROVIDES GRANTS TO MISSIONARY ORGANISATIONS FOR THEIR DEVELOPMENT WORK IN AFRICA, ASIA AND SOUTH AMERICA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PARTNER: Salesian Sisters PROJECT: The aim is to provide equitable access to sanitation hygiene (WASH) services to enhance health, dignity and quality of life for the marginalised and vulnerable groups in Sandali ward, Temeke, Dar es Salaam, Tanzania. This project specifically targets women and children with disabilities. Key activities include both hardware (construction and rehabilitation of accessible sanitation and water facilities) and software (capacity-building, awareness campaigns, and behaviour change programs) to ensure sustainable impact.</narrative>
  </description>
